<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a bug in the `parse_atxheader` function in `src/document.c`. This function calls the header callback (which is set to `toc_header` in the fuzzer) with a `NULL` `content` argument. The `toc_header` function does not handle the case where `content` is `NULL` and attempts to dereference it, leading to a segmentation fault.

A potential fix would be to add a null check in the `toc_header` function in `src/html.c` before dereferencing the `content` pointer. For example:

```c
void
toc_header(hoedown_buffer *ob, const hoedown_buffer *content, const hoedown_buffer *attr, int level, void *data)
{
if (content) {
rndr_header_id(ob, content->data, content->size, 1, data);
}
}
```
This would prevent the crash when `parse_atxheader` calls the callback with a `NULL` content.
</crash-analysis>

